{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-64222","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122886","text":"delegatic"}]},{"id":"blk-64223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122887","text":"OS-006 Governance Shim — authorization kernel for the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]},{"id":"blk-64224","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122888","text":"Issues signed, expiring "},{"id":"spn-122889","marks":["code"],"text":"AuthorizationBlock"},{"id":"spn-122890","text":"s to destructive edges in GRASP "},{"id":"spn-122891","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.*"},{"id":"spn-122892","text":" replay flows. Policy-based, deny-by-default, pluggable policy store."}]},{"id":"blk-64225","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122893","text":"Status"}]},{"id":"blk-64226","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122894","marks":["bold"],"text":"Library:"},{"id":"spn-122895","text":" v0.1.0 production-ready"}]}],"id":"blk-64227","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122896","marks":["bold"],"text":"Tests:"},{"id":"spn-122897","text":" 42/42 (25 unit + 3 integration + 14 MCP tool tests) + 2 body-os end-to-end integration tests"}]}],"id":"blk-64229","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64232","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122898","marks":["bold"],"text":"Storage:"},{"id":"spn-122899","text":" in-memory ETS-backed "},{"id":"spn-122900","marks":["code"],"text":"PolicyStore"},{"id":"spn-122901","text":" — Postgres-backed adapter is a future additive release"}]}],"id":"blk-64231","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64234","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122902","marks":["bold"],"text":"MCP server:"},{"id":"spn-122903","text":" shipped — 6 tools on the "},{"id":"spn-122904","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic"},{"id":"spn-122905","text":" namespace (put/get/list/delete policy + authorize + verify) with Anubis stdio/HTTP transport"}]}],"id":"blk-64233","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122906","marks":["bold"],"text":"Deployment:"},{"id":"spn-122907","text":" "},{"id":"spn-122908","marks":["code"],"text":"fly.toml"},{"id":"spn-122909","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-122910","marks":["code"],"text":"Dockerfile"},{"id":"spn-122911","text":" ready for Fly.io ("},{"id":"spn-122912","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic-mcp"},{"id":"spn-122913","text":", port 4400)"}]}],"id":"blk-64235","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-64237","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122914","text":"MCP surface"}]},{"id":"blk-64238","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"delegatic_put_policy       — register or replace a Policy\ndelegatic_get_policy       — look up a Policy by id\ndelegatic_list_policies    — list every registered Policy\ndelegatic_delete_policy    — remove a Policy\ndelegatic_authorize        — issue a fresh AuthorizationBlock\ndelegatic_verify           — verify a block's HMAC signature + TTL"},{"id":"blk-64239","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122915","text":"Remote agents (body-browser-mcp, body-os-mcp, FleetPrompt's InstallEngine, Graphonomous replay flows) call "},{"id":"spn-122916","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic_authorize"},{"id":"spn-122917","text":" to obtain the fresh blocks they need for destructive edges per GRASP §4.4."}]},{"id":"blk-64240","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122918","text":"This is the "},{"id":"spn-122919","marks":["italic"],"text":"authorization kernel"},{"id":"spn-122920","text":" — the minimum needed to close the GRASP destructive-edge loop. The full Delegatic spec ("},{"id":"spn-122921","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic.com/docs/spec/"},{"id":"spn-122922","text":") layers on org trees, memberships, effective-policy computation, and a LiveView dashboard; those are future work."}]},{"id":"blk-64241","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122923","text":"Contract"}]},{"id":"blk-64242","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# 1. Register a policy\n:ok =\n  Delegatic.put_policy(\n    Delegatic.Policy.new(%{\n      policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n      allow_actions: [\"file_write\", \"shell_exec\"],\n      deny_actions: [\"file_delete\"],\n      agents: [\"ops-agent\"],\n      max_ttl_seconds: 300\n    })\n  )\n\n# 2. Directly request authorization for one action\n{:ok, block} =\n  Delegatic.authorize(\n    action_type: \"file_write\",\n    policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n    agent_id: \"ops-agent\",\n    approved_by: \"supervisor@acme\"\n  )\n\n# 3. Or build a function ready for the GRASP Replay `:authorizer` slot\nauthorizer =\n  Delegatic.authorizer_for(\n    policy_id: \"delegatic://ws-42/ops\",\n    approved_by: \"supervisor@acme\",\n    agent_id: \"ops-agent\"\n  )\n\n# 4. Wire it into body-os replay\nBodyOs.Replay.execute(session, trace, authorizer: authorizer)"},{"id":"blk-64243","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122924","text":"AuthorizationBlock"}]},{"id":"blk-64244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122925","text":"Every issued block carries:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-64246","spans":[{"id":"spn-122926","text":"Field"}]},{"id":"blk-64247","spans":[{"id":"spn-122927","text":"Example"}]}],"id":"blk-64245","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-64248","spans":[{"id":"spn-122928","marks":["code"],"text":"policy_id"}]},{"id":"blk-64249","spans":[{"id":"spn-122929","marks":["code"],"text":"\"delegatic://ws-42/ops\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-64250","spans":[{"id":"spn-122930","marks":["code"],"text":"approved_by"}]},{"id":"blk-64251","spans":[{"id":"spn-122931","marks":["code"],"text":"\"supervisor@acme\""}]}],[{"id":"blk-64252","spans":[{"id":"spn-122932","marks":["code"],"text":"approved_at"}]},{"id":"blk-64253","spans":[{"id":"spn-122933","text":"ISO8601 UTC"}]}],[{"id":"blk-64254","spans":[{"id":"spn-122934","marks":["code"],"text":"expires_at"}]},{"id":"blk-64255","spans":[{"id":"spn-122935","text":"ISO8601 UTC (capped at "},{"id":"spn-122936","marks":["code"],"text":"policy.max_ttl_seconds"},{"id":"spn-122937","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-64256","spans":[{"id":"spn-122938","marks":["code"],"text":"authorization_token"}]},{"id":"blk-64257","spans":[{"id":"spn-122939","marks":["code"],"text":"\"sha256:<64-hex>\""},{"id":"spn-122940","text":" — HMAC over the other fields"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-64258","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122941","text":"The token is "},{"id":"spn-122942","marks":["italic"],"text":"tamper-evident"},{"id":"spn-122943","text":", not secret — any consumer can call "},{"id":"spn-122944","marks":["code"],"text":"Delegatic.AuthorizationBlock.verify/1"},{"id":"spn-122945","text":" to detect forgery or expiration."}]},{"id":"blk-64259","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122946","text":"The HMAC key lives in "},{"id":"spn-122947","marks":["code"],"text":"config :delegatic, :hmac_key"},{"id":"spn-122948","text":". A per-process random fallback is used when unset (fine for tests, unsafe for prod)."}]},{"id":"blk-64260","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122949","text":"Policy semantics"}]},{"id":"blk-64261","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122950","marks":["bold"],"text":"`action in deny_actions`"},{"id":"spn-122951","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-122952","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :denied_by_policy}"}]}],"id":"blk-64262","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122953","marks":["bold"],"text":"`agents` set and `agent_id` not in it"},{"id":"spn-122954","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-122955","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :agent_not_allowed}"}]}],"id":"blk-64264","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64267","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122956","marks":["bold"],"text":"`action not in allow_actions`"},{"id":"spn-122957","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-122958","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, :not_in_allowlist}"},{"id":"spn-122959","text":" (deny-by-default)"}]}],"id":"blk-64266","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64269","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122960","text":"Otherwise → "},{"id":"spn-122961","marks":["code"],"text":":ok"}]}],"id":"blk-64268","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-64270","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122962","text":"Wiring Delegatic into GRASP replay"}]},{"id":"blk-64271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122963","text":"The GRASP spec §4.4 requires that every destructive replay edge obtain a "},{"id":"spn-122964","marks":["italic"],"text":"fresh"},{"id":"spn-122965","text":" authorization — prior authorization does not carry. Delegatic's "},{"id":"spn-122966","marks":["code"],"text":"authorizer_for/1"},{"id":"spn-122967","text":" returns a function that re-issues a new block on every call, producing exactly the semantics GRASP demands:"}]},{"id":"blk-64272","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"# Recorded trace: destructive edges carry OLD authorization blocks\n# Replay stripper: body-os.Replay strips them before dispatch\n# Delegatic authorizer: fresh block for every edge that makes it through policy\n# Session: enforces the destructive-action gate on the fresh block"},{"id":"blk-64273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122968","text":"See "},{"id":"spn-122969","marks":["code"],"text":"body-os/test/delegatic_integration_test.exs"},{"id":"spn-122970","text":" for the end-to-end test that exercises this flow — both the success path (allowlist policy → replay succeeds) and the failure path (readonly policy → replay halts with "},{"id":"spn-122971","marks":["code"],"text":"reason: \"authorization_failure\""},{"id":"spn-122972","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-64274","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122973","text":"Running the suite"}]},{"id":"blk-64275","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"mix deps.get\nmix test"},{"id":"blk-64276","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122974","text":"References"}]},{"id":"blk-64277","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122975","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic.com/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-122976","text":" — full v0.2 spec (organizations, memberships, effective policy, dashboard)"}]}],"id":"blk-64278","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64281","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122977","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience.org/docs/spec/OS-011-EMBODIMENT.md"},{"id":"spn-122978","text":" §4.4 — AuthorizationBlock contract"}]}],"id":"blk-64280","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-64283","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122979","marks":["code"],"text":"body-os/"},{"id":"spn-122980","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-122981","marks":["code"],"text":"body-browser/"},{"id":"spn-122982","text":" — GRASP providers whose Replay flows consume Delegatic authorizers"}]}],"id":"blk-64282","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-64284","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-122983","text":"License"}]},{"id":"blk-64285","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-122984","text":"Apache-2.0"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierajw3dhejgudlmitxgqjl6lzxbtl47qgqebmotvj6lgs4r6xou5ura","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}